 },
 "summary": "A 50 Ω surface-mount high pass filter built in LTCC ceramic, with seven sections, a passband of 780 to 2800 MHz and a 740 MHz cut-off. It rejects at least 40 dB at 430 MHz and 20 dB at 550 MHz, and takes up to 7 W of RF input in the passband at +25 °C. The body is a hermetically sealed FV1206 case, 3.20 × 1.60 mm. Uses named for it are sub-harmonic rejection, transmitters and receivers, and lab work.",
