 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Seven filter sections in low-temperature co-fired ceramic, hermetically sealed, with stable behaviour over temperature. Between RF IN and RF OUT the internal network is a ladder of series capacitors with shunt inductors to ground."
  },
  {
   "topic": "DC on the ports",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Where either port carries a DC voltage, put coupling capacitors in series with it, or use the \"D\" suffix version, whose ports show more than 100 MΩ to ground."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power handling",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Up to 7 W of RF input in the passband at +25 °C ambient, falling linearly to 3 W at +100 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Test board and layout",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Specifications are measured on demo board TB-HFCN-740+, layout PL-137. Its ports are coplanar waveguide with a 0.038\" trace and 0.013\" gaps on Rogers RO4350B 0.020\" ± 0.0015\" thick, 1/2 oz copper on each side; another laminate may need a different trace width and gap. The bottom side is one continuous ground plane, and the top ground carries eight 0.015\" plated through holes. Copper outside the pads is covered by solder mask; the pads are left bare."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Land pattern",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The suggested land pattern has one end pad for each RF port and two ground pads between them, each ground pad carrying a plated through hole of diameter N. Its dimensions hold to ±0.002\"."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Marked F7. The index area on top identifies pin 1; alphanumeric markings may appear on top, and pad shape may vary."
  }
 ],
